   "A": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 465 of the laws of 1994, amending chapter 285 of the\nlaws of 1891 relating to charging a fee for admission to the New York\nBotanical Garden, in relation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7556",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7556-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 465 of 1994",
    "lawSection": "New York City",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7556A\n\nSPONSOR: BIAGGI\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 465 of the laws of 1994, amending chapter 285 of\nthe laws of 1891 relating to charging a fee for admission to the New\nYork Botanical Garden, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to give the New York Botanical Garden\nauthorization to charge or not charge an admission fee.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one extends the expiration date authorizing the New York Botan-\nical Garden to charge a fee for admission by the general public to help\nsustain the organization's operations and botanical exhibits.\n\nSection two sets forth an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe New York Botanical Garden (NYBG) charges nominal and varying fees\nfor admission to certain exhibits of this organization. They must be\nauthorized to continue to do so in order to remain open to the public\nand a financially viable organization that can continue to host new\nliving exhibits. This legislation will provide NYBG with parity among\nother organizations that are not required to pass legislation yearly to\ncharge admission.  The following organizations charge for admission and\ndo not require legislation to do so:\n\n \nBRONX:\nBronx Academy of Arts and Dance\nBronx River Arts Center\nLehman Center for the Performing Arts\nHostos Center for Performing Arts\nPregones Theater\nWave Hill\n \nMANHATTAN:\n\nAmerican Museum of Natural History\nCarnegie Hall\nEl Museo del Barrio\nLincoln Center for the Performing Arts\nMoMa\nMetropolitan Museum of Art\nMetropolitan Opera\nMuseum of the City of New York\nNew York City Ballet\nNew York Historical Society\nNew York Philharmonic\nPublic Theater\nStudio Museum in Harlem\nGuggenheim\nThe Whitney\n \nBROOKLYN:\n\nBrooklyn Academy of Music (BAM) Brooklyn Children's Museum\nBrooklyn Museum\nBrooklyn Botanic Garden\nNY Aquarium\n \nQUEENS:\n\nFlushing Town Hall\nMuseum of the Moving Image\nQueens Botanical Garden\nQueens Museum Queens Theater\n \nSTATEN ISLAND:\n\nSnug Harbor and Cultural Center Staten Island Children's Museum Staten\nIsland Historical Society Staten Island Museum\nStaten Island Zoo\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019: passed Senate and Assembly, vetoed (memo 148)\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
